  "limits": [
    "C1/C2 delegate to the measured revision's tools; measure.py does not independently reimplement those checks.",
    "C2's census facet is the `.ufo/gates/c1-census-v10.py` blob at REV run with `--root LANE`. The instrument reads the LANE working tree and the live host client configs, not REV's blobs, so its verdict is a live reading made by that revision's code, not a revision-scoped snapshot of text.",
    "C1/C2 require the tool's echoed `rev` to equal the resolved commit when it is present; a mismatch is could-not-evaluate because the count would not be at REV.",
    "C3 `labels_frozen` counts committed `predictions/<label>.prediction.json` blobs whose `carrier.sha256` is a 64-hex string. Freeze order (prediction commit before any carrier run commit) is not verified here; that is the decision rule's receipt-validate binding gate.",
    "C3 prefers runs/pass2 when present, otherwise pass 1. Raw compare counts copy recorded all_match/exit values, not a semantic log judgment. bound_validated additionally re-runs REV's validator/pins on each receipt only after its current bytes equal the committed receipt blob; validator reads the recorded absolute live paths, so this field is time-dependent.",
    "A count of 0 is a measured zero (no matching artifact at that revision), not an error.",
    "Tools are imported from temporary revision copies (trusted lane code, not an OS sandbox). C3 bound validation and C2 live census read the working tree as explicitly described above. No carrier is executed.",
    "Import-time and call-time Python stdout/stderr are captured; a tool that writes straight to the process file descriptors (an uncaptured child) is outside that capture."
  ],
